A||||19||Eric||Searching for Commonality (need advice)||||1||
Z||000000||Eric||06-08-2001||08:30 PM||||So I've been talking to this girl lately, and I'm having a hard time trying to make conversation with her.  The worst part is she has a personality similar to mine (something rare, I think).  I find myself trying so hard to conjure up something to say, that I completely come out of myself and don't act like I normally do.  I don't have the same problem acting like myself around other girls, and never to this extent with girls I like.  I just need to find a way to stop psyching myself out about this, and find some common ground with her.  Any advice?||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||06-08-2001||08:32 PM||||You talk to girls?!?!?!  <P>OK OK J/K, sorry, Umm if you can't think of anything to say and feel weird around her, how do you know your personalities are the same? I've been in that situation where you just don't know what to say to a person and you feel dumb, and it just doesn't magically come, unless you happen to have something in common that both of you are passionate about. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||06-08-2001||08:46 PM||||just an idea. try a movie. if she'll go you can talk a little at the beginning, then be with her without really having to say much while the movies on. then you have if nothing else the movie to talk about when it's over. maybe more conversation can branch off from there.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||06-08-2001||08:46 PM||||like cars  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> or ummm.. how many times you brush your hair in one day? How many insane relatives you have? I dunno, I dont talk to girls.. they seem to dislike me.<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe Auto 4Banger - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR>AIM: WookieeNC||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric||06-08-2001||08:54 PM||||I may be better off if I didn't talk to girls, Lisa.  I'm driven by much the same thing you are  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Thing is, I've known her for some time, so I know what she's like.  I just never really talked to her before, and I get the feeling it's uncomfortable for both of us.  We're such social people otherwise, it's strange to have two seemingly extroverted people sharing silence.  What can I talk about with her?||||reg||1
