Z||000009||fierojunky||06-11-2001||01:19 PM||||Just be yourself.  Have a good friend around when you talk to her.  You'll be more comfortable with a friend there and once you guys get talking your friend can leave.  And if you take a friend like anyone of mine they will definitely let you know if you’re not being yourself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Eric||06-11-2001||01:42 PM||||Thanks everybody.  I saw her again the other day, and now we are getting along beautifully.  All that anxiety I once had is just a distant memory.<P>Fierojunky, my friends are all assholes.  They would ruin everything on purpose just for a laugh.  I really hate those guys  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||06-11-2001||01:52 PM||||The answer to you question is simple. you talk to her about what almost everyone likes to talk about - themselves (herself, not yourself!).<P>  Ask her about herself. talk to her about stuff she is intersted in and let her tell you what she thinks, what she feels, what she wants to do, how she spends her time...<P>  The one thing everyone is an expert on is themselves - let her do most of the talking.<P>   then when she is alone later she will be thinking to herself - wow - that guy is so great - what a great listener he is - hes the kinda guy you can really talk to. He was really intereseted in ME!<P>  second (I know this is gonna sound corny, but do it anyway) go to the library or bookstore and get Dale Carnigies book "how to win friends and influence people" and read the whole thing.<P>   it is not a bunch of nonsense some old guy made up off the top of his head. He spent years and years RESEARCHING how sucessful people have made their mark on the world - and the most important assest he discovered is interpersonal skills<P>  and he explains them all to you. The fact that you can sit next to an attractive interesting lady and have nothing to say to her PROVES you need to read this book.<P>  IT WILL CHANGE YOUR LIFE!<P>  and thats all I have to say about that.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Voytek||06-11-2001||05:21 PM||||Umm, maybe you should just let your hads do the work.  That way you don't need to talk at all.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||JSocha||06-11-2001||05:41 PM||||May want to pick up the audio tape "Men are from Mars/Women are from Venus", pop it into your tape deck when driving around if you can or can get ahold of the tapes.  If your into readin, then perhaps the book.<P>Dale Carnagie...people actually still listen to him??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ken Wittlief||06-13-2001||10:15 AM||||yes, technology has changed, but human nature has been pretty much the same for the last 6,000 years.<P>  Carnegies book is based on research going way back to people like washington, franklin, Lincoln, right up to contemporary people of his time.<P>  its all still valid - esp his first rule: never criticize someone if you are trying to establish a relationship with them.<P>  if you want to know why - read the book - libraries have tons of copies - free wisdom!||||reg||1
Z||000015||AusFiero||06-13-2001||10:17 AM||||Sounds like maybe yous best skip the words and get straight to the action. You will have plenty to talk about then.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000016||Ken Wittlief||06-13-2001||10:34 AM||||one last plug for 'how to win friends and influence people' <BR> <BR>at least a few people told me I should read the book when I was young (not just me, that everyone should read it).<P>  I thought, yeah right! I dont need that - If someone tells you how to influence people then you are not being yourself, you are a phoney, right?<P>   It wasnt till I was 34, and I was between jobs, that a person at a professional recruiting agency GAVE me a copy of the book, and said "we tell everyone to read this, there are things in here that will make job hunting more successful..."<P>  so I finally read it when I was 34. Then I thought DAMN! I wish I had read this back when I was 12, like people told me to.<P>   Its not very often you can spend a few hours doing something that really will change the whole rest of your life. So now, when ever someone tells me, This will change your life, I at least look into it.<P>  and that whole thing about being phoney - you didnt learn how to eat by yourself, or how to get dressed, or how to speak, or how to do math - someone taught you. So why should developing interpersonal skills be any different?<P>  Young people often feel, "I want to be ME! I want to be my real self"<P>  when you get older you start feeling more like, "Ok, i've wasted enough time trying to figure this out by myself, someone explain to me how it works, please!"<P>  and thats all I have to say about that||||reg||1
Z||000017||RiceCooker||06-13-2001||03:13 PM||||From "American Pie"<P>OZ: All you have to do is ask them questions and listen what they have to say n $hit.<P>Stiffler: Gee, I dunno, that sounds like a lotta work.<P>I've been talking to this one girl for a while too. It's so tough because no matter what i say, she doesn't say much back.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I mean i start out as real nice and friendly but after a while i just become so impatient with her and end up deflating her and putting her back in the closet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>So then I just phone up my other girlfriends<P>Palmela Handerson and her five sisters <BR>hahahahahaha I couldn't resist<BR>||||reg||1
